CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Was KNOWNBUG; fixed by two changes: (1) N5008 [expr.prim.id.dtor] +
[class.dtor]/1,6 -- the explicit destructor call notation on a class
whose destructor is implicitly declared and trivial (no synthesized
destructor symbol under CBMC's POD gate) now uses the same no-op dummy
as scalar pseudo-destructor calls, so the destructibility SFINAE probe
`decltype(declval<T&>().~T())` resolves; (2) the ~_Tp destructor-name
substitution now prefers the template-map binding that designates the
CURRENT class scope ([expr.prim.id.dtor]/2) instead of an arbitrary
same-short-name binding, and extracts the class's unqualified name
ANGLE-AWARE (a naive rfind("::") landed inside a template instance's
arguments, spelling e.g. `~allocator` for basic_string).  Header-free
skeleton of libstdc++'s std::optional<std::string> (see
cpp17_optional_string, fixed by the same changes).
